# Environment
#
# Deny every .env variant, then let the committed templates back in. The old
# list named the three shapes someone had thought of — .env, .env.local,
# .env.*.local — so anything else was tracked by default. A probe env written
# during an investigation (.env.probe) sat in a worktree holding five real
# 66-character secrets, one `git add -A` away from the history.
#
# The negation is what keeps the six *.example templates committed; they are
# the documentation for these variables and must stay visible.
.env
.env.*
!.env*.example

